(* Copyright 2026 nfltr
   SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

   e2ee_tcp.pv: end-to-end encrypted TCP sessions, organisation mode, the
   only mode (lane ORG2; pins deleted by lane ORGCUT: nfltr
   docs/decisions/org-enrolment-2026-11-09.md "Migration: a hard cut").
   A tcp service in organisation mode (agent.Service.Org, AllowGroups;
   Config.TCPE2EEOrg for a tunnel) ends TLS with its machine certificate,
   issued under the organisation's root; a client names the machine (nfltr
   dial web/pg, to: web/pg on a connect: mapping) and checks the chain and
   the name; the service admits a client certificate under the same root,
   in one of its allow_group groups, neither expired nor on the issuer's
   CRL. Its plaintext goes only to the target the agent fixed (its table's,
   --forward's), and each end of the session is the peer's own, never the
   relay's cut. spec/proverif/README.md "e2ee_tcp.pv".

   A service and a client are each in their mode by their own
   configuration, never by the relay (the downgrade mutants below).

   The attacker owns the relay(s): the open, its E2Ee flag and target, the
   answer, the certificate a session presents, every byte, a stream's raw
   end; two relays are one attacker. It holds the keys of: eve (enrolled,
   live, group web: not the service's group), lost (group db, revoked: its
   serial on the CRL), old (group db, expired), and two of web's own (an
   expired one and a revoked one). nfltr's enrol.pv proves who can get a
   certificate of the organisation (only the issuer under the root, for a
   token's own name); here the organisation's signing key is one private
   key, orgk, and a certificate is its signature over (name, group, key,
   serial, validity). The CRL the verifier holds lists serWebRev and
   serLost; validity live or expired is the verifier's clock against
   NotAfter. Time and re-checks (a session ends at Identity.Until, a newer
   CRL cuts what it lists) are nfltr spec/enrol/Enrol.tla's
   NoExpiredSession and RevocationBound, not here.

   TLS 1.3 is not re-proven: a client that checked the server's
   certificate shares a fresh key only with that key's holder (Cremers et
   al., IEEE S&P 2017, Tamarin; Bhargavan et al., IEEE S&P 2017,
   ProVerif/CryptoVerif). TLS 1.3 CertificateVerify is the client's
   signature over a hash of the session key and the server's key (the
   transcript); crypto/tls checks it against the certificate's key. A TLS
   record carries its content type: application data (appData) or the
   close_notify alert (closeAlert); a stream's raw end (rawEnd: the
   transport's EOF, which the relay can produce between any two records)
   carries none. A record is bound to its place in its direction's stream
   (the sequence number in the AEAD nonce): the model's close record names
   the bytes it follows. crypto/tls reports both a close_notify and a raw
   end as io.EOF; tlsend.Conn tells them apart.

   Direct paths (lane DIRECTPATH, a design: nfltr
   docs/decisions/direct-paths-2026-11-11.md; no code yet). Once the
   session's TLS is up, its client may move the session's bytes (the same
   TLS records, under the same session key) to a direct QUIC connection
   to an address the relay hands it (a candidate, a QAD reply): whoever
   holds that address answers, so the address is the attacker's. The
   client takes the direct connection only if the answer's certificate
   passes the same check as the session's (chain, name, NotAfter, CRL)
   and both ends prove the session: each sends, inside the QUIC session,
   an exporter of the TLS session bound to the QUIC session's key
   (tokC, tokS below). The agent binds a direct connection to a session
   only on that session's token. Queries 21-26; mutants direct-*.

   Direct paths under a group dial (lane DIRECTGROUP: nfltr
   docs/decisions/service-discovery-2026-11-12.md section 4 "Direct paths
   under a group dial"): the group-dial client names no machine, so its
   direct check takes the name the session's certificate carries: the
   direct answer must name the machine whose agent holds the session, not
   any machine of the group (36; mutant group-direct-no-name-check, the
   group's check on the direct answer: alone it holds, the tokens bind the
   session; with direct-no-token the relay moves the session to another
   instance, mal, 36). Which agent the control exchange and a re-attach
   reach is the relay's routing (candidates and addresses are already the
   attacker's): a wrong one is a denial.

   Re-attach (gap G2): each attach (a switch) is a fresh stream, an epoch,
   opened by the client with OPEN(epoch, token). ep1 is the direct
   connection; when it dies the client opens a new relayed stream (ep2),
   and later another (ep3), each with the token of that epoch: an
   exporter of the session's TLS bound to the client's role and the epoch
   (tokR; the exporter, h((k, ns)), takes the server's random ns, as TLS
   1.3's does: the model's k is the client's alone, so without ns the
   relay replaying the client's handshake to a second agent session would
   give two agent sessions one exporter). On a relayed stream the relay sees OPEN and can replay an
   earlier epoch's on a new stream, rewriting its epoch field. The agent
   has one acceptor per epoch of a session and attaches a stream at epoch
   e only on the client's token for e (27; mutant token-no-epoch, the
   token without the epoch: the replay attaches). Either way the bytes on
   a re-attached stream are the session's TLS records, secret (28): a
   replay is a denial only.
   Services by name (lane SVCBIND: nfltr
   docs/decisions/service-discovery-2026-11-12.md section 4). Web serves
   a second organisation service, vault (published under no group), and
   machine mal (group db, a live certificate, the relay's choice to route
   to) serves a pg published under ops, not db. A client offers one ALPN
   protocol naming what it dialled: alpnM(agent, service) for a machine
   dial (nfltr-svc/<agent>/<service>), alpnG(service, group) for a group
   dial (nfltr-svc/<service>@<group>); the offer travels in the clear (the
   model does not lean on the transcript covering it), the agent's choice
   comes back in EncryptedExtensions under the session key. The agent
   accepts an offer only for the service the session was routed to (its
   process's svc) and, for alpnG, a group it publishes that service under
   and its certificate's OU holds, else no_application_protocol; the client
   requires the negotiated protocol to be its offer. A group-dial client
   (GClient) checks the chain, OU contains the group, NotAfter and the CRL,
   no name. Queries 30-35; mutants client-no-alpn-check,
   agent-no-alpn-check, group-dial-no-group-check, agent-no-publish-check.
     BIND:org.service     the ALPN name: offered, accepted by the agent, checked negotiated
     BIND:org.group       the group: in the certificate's OU (the client's check; the agent's own)
     BIND:org.publish     the agent serves <service>@<group> only for a service it publishes under group

   Datagram services (lane UDP1: nfltr docs/decisions/nf1-udp-2026-11-14.md
   section 3). A service has a kind, stream or datagram, and one name may
   serve both (dns over tcp and udp): web serves pg as a stream and as a
   datagram service, each published under db. The ALPN carries the kind
   (nfltr-svc/ for a stream, nfltr-dg/ for a datagram service, both dial
   forms); the agent accepts an offer only of its service's kind, so a
   relay cannot route a stream client to the datagram service or the
   reverse (42; mutant agent-ignores-kind; client-no-alpn-check: the relay
   rewrites the offer's kind; the attack needs one name under both
   kinds, else the service name already refuses it). Once direct, a datagram session's datagrams
   ride the direct connection as QUIC DATAGRAM frames under its keys,
   tagged with the attach; the agent hands one to a session only on a
   connection bound to it (38-41; mutant dgram-tag-unbound), as
   cap_address.pv 21-24.
     BIND:org.kind        the ALPN's kind prefix: offered, accepted by the agent only for its service's kind
     BIND:dgram.tag       a frame's tag: a session attached on this connection, up

   Bindings (direct-paths doc "E2EE"; each gets a refusal row in the
   code's bindings test when the code lands):
     BIND:direct.cert     the direct answer's certificate checked as the session's
     BIND:direct.name     ... names the machine the client named (a group dial: the session's certificate's)
     BIND:direct.token    tokC/tokS: an exporter of the session's TLS key
     BIND:direct.quic     ... bound to the direct QUIC session's key
     BIND:direct.role     ... the sender's role (labC, labS)
     BIND:direct.epoch    ... and the attach's epoch (tokC/tokS at ep1, tokR at ep2, ep3)

   Code (nfltr = github.com/nfltr/nfltr; the rest github.com/nfltr/relay):
     client/orgid/verify.go Verifier.Check               chain to the root, name, groups, CRL, NotAfter
     client/orgid/identity.go ClientTLS, GroupClientTLS  the client's check of a machine by name, of a group dial by OU
     client/agent/org.go Org.CheckClient                 the service's check (client/orgid Identity behind it)
     client/agent/org.go orgServerConfig                 RequireAnyClientCert + VerifyConnection, no other mode
     client/agent/org.go checkOrgService                 e2ee On needs Org and a group (services, the tunnel)
     client/agent/services.go resolve                    an org service takes no plain session; no other tcp service an E2EE one
     client/agent/session_plan.go planOpen               target: the table's, --forward's; never the relay's
     client/agent/agent.go New                           TCPE2EEOnly without TCPForwardAddr: Connect fails
     client/agent/org.go serveE2EETCP, client/tlsend, link peerlink.Join:
                                                         a stream that ends without the peer's close_notify
                                                         is a reset; the target's reset is one to the client
     nfltr cmd/nfltr/internal/transportcli/org_session.go the client: ServerName <name>.<org>.internal, the check;
                                                         its mode is its own (enrolled: organisation), never the answer's
     nfltr .../tcp_connect_session.go Pump, tlsSession.Reset: the local application's reset likewise
     client/agent/service_alpn.go                        the ALPN protocols: the agent's choice, the client's check *)

free c: channel.

type skey.
type pkey.
fun pk(skey): pkey.
fun aenc(bitstring, pkey): bitstring.
reduc forall m: bitstring, k: skey; adec(aenc(m, pk(k)), k) = m.
fun senc(bitstring, bitstring): bitstring.
reduc forall m: bitstring, k: bitstring; sdec(senc(m, k), k) = m.
fun sign(bitstring, skey): bitstring.
reduc forall m: bitstring, k: skey; checksign(sign(m, k), pk(k)) = m.
reduc forall m: bitstring, k: skey; getmsg(sign(m, k)) = m.    (* a certificate's contents are public *)
fun h(bitstring): bitstring.

const svcAddr: bitstring.                     (* the target the agent means: its table's, --forward's *)
const c2s, s2c: bitstring.                    (* TLS keys each direction apart *)
const appData, closeAlert, rawEnd: bitstring.
const answerOK, answerPlain: bitstring.       (* the relay's word: accepted; "the service is plain" *)
const live, expired: bitstring.
const nameWeb, nameCli, nameEve, nameLost, nameOld: bitstring.
const grpDb, grpWeb: bitstring.
const serWeb, serWebOld, serWebRev, serCli, serEve, serLost, serOld: bitstring.
const noCert: bitstring.                      (* a client that presents no organisation certificate *)
const labC, labS: bitstring.                  (* the direct token's roles: the client's, the agent's *)
const ep1, ep2, ep3, noEpoch: bitstring.      (* attach epochs: ep1 direct, ep2 and ep3 relayed re-attaches *)
const nameMal, serMal, grpOps, noGroup: bitstring.
const svcPg, svcVault: bitstring.             (* service names *)
const eeTag: bitstring.                       (* EncryptedExtensions: the negotiated ALPN protocol *)
fun alpnM(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring): bitstring [data].   (* <kind prefix><agent>/<service> *)
fun alpnG(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring): bitstring [data].   (* <kind prefix><service>@<group> *)
const kindS, kindDg: bitstring.               (* the ALPN prefixes: nfltr-svc/ a stream, nfltr-dg/ a datagram service *)
const labD: bitstring.                        (* a datagram frame's label *)

free orgk: skey [private].                    (* the organisation: root, then issuer (enrol.pv) *)
free skWeb, skCli, skMal: skey [private].
free payload: bitstring [private].            (* what the client sends machine web *)
free vData: bitstring [private].              (* what a client sends web/vault *)
free gData: bitstring [private].              (* what the group-dial client sends pg@db *)
free svcData: bitstring [private].            (* what web's service answers an admitted client *)
free dirData: bitstring [private].            (* what the client sends on a direct connection it took *)
free attData: bitstring [private].            (* what the client sends on a relayed stream it re-attached *)
free uData: bitstring [private].              (* what a datagram client sends web/pg's datagram service *)
free dgData: bitstring [private].             (* a datagram a client sends on its direct connection *)

(* The direct answer's name check: the machine the client named (a machine
   dial) or its session's certificate names (a group dial, grouped).
   group-direct-no-name-check: a group dial takes any machine of the group. *)
letfun directNameOK(dn: bitstring, dg: bitstring, want: bitstring, grouped: bool) = (dn = want). (* NOT:group-direct-no-name-check *)
letfun directNameOK(dn: bitstring, dg: bitstring, want: bitstring, grouped: bool) = if grouped = true then (dg = grpDb) else (dn = want). (* ONLY:group-direct-no-name-check *)

(* The epoch a token binds; token-no-epoch: none. *)
letfun tokEpoch(e: bitstring) = e. (* NOT:token-no-epoch *)
letfun tokEpoch(e: bitstring) = noEpoch. (* ONLY:token-no-epoch *)

(* The agent's ALPN choice for a session routed to its service svc,
   published under pub, its certificate's OU ou: the machine dial of
   itself and that service, or that service under a group the OU holds
   and the service is published under. agent-no-publish-check: any group
   the OU holds. *)
letfun published(g: bitstring, pub: bitstring) = (g = pub). (* NOT:agent-no-publish-check *)
letfun published(g: bitstring, pub: bitstring) = true. (* ONLY:agent-no-publish-check *)
letfun kindOK(ok: bitstring, kind: bitstring) = (ok = kind). (* NOT:agent-ignores-kind *)
letfun kindOK(ok: bitstring, kind: bitstring) = true. (* ONLY:agent-ignores-kind *)
letfun alpnOK(offer: bitstring, kind: bitstring, name: bitstring, svc: bitstring, pub: bitstring, ou: bitstring) =
  let alpnM(ok, =name, =svc) = offer in kindOK(ok, kind) else
  let alpnG(ok, =svc, g) = offer in (if g = ou then (if kindOK(ok, kind) then published(g, pub) else false) else false) else false.

event ClientAccepted(bitstring).                       (* the serial of the server certificate the client took *)
event ClientSent(bitstring, bitstring).                (* its own serial, its bytes *)
event ClientRecv(bitstring, bitstring).                (* session key, response *)
event AgentSent(bitstring, bitstring).                 (* session key, response *)
event ServiceGot(bitstring, bitstring).                (* the admitted client's serial, its bytes *)
event ClientEnded(bitstring, bitstring).               (* the client's close_notify after its bytes *)
event ClientCleanEnd(bitstring, bitstring).            (* session key, response: a clean end delivered *)
event AgentEnded(bitstring, bitstring).                (* session key, response: its close_notify *)
event ServiceCleanEnd(bitstring, bitstring).           (* the service's half close: the client's serial, its bytes *)
event TargetEnded(bitstring, bitstring).               (* session key, response: the target's clean end *)
event TargetAborted(bitstring, bitstring).             (* ... the target's reset *)
event AppEnded(bitstring, bitstring).                  (* the client's local application's clean end after its bytes *)
event AppAborted(bitstring, bitstring).                (* ... its reset *)
event ClientDirectOffer(bitstring, bitstring).         (* session key, direct QUIC key: the client's token sent *)
event ClientDirect(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring).   (* session key, direct key, the answer's serial: taken *)
event AgentDirect(bitstring, bitstring).               (* session key, direct key: bound to that session *)
event DirectTaken(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bitstring, bool). (* session key, direct key, the answer's name, the session's machine, a group dial *)
event ClientAttach(bitstring, bitstring).              (* session key, epoch: the client's OPEN sent *)
event AgentAttach(bitstring, bitstring).               (* session key, epoch: the agent attached that stream *)
event Dialled(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring).        (* a machine dial: agent, service, the bytes it sends *)
event Publishes(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring).      (* an agent: machine, service, the group it publishes it under *)
event Served(bitstring, bitstring, bitstring).         (* an agent: machine, service, the bytes its service got *)
event GClientRecv(bitstring, bitstring).               (* the group-dial client: session key, response *)
event Dials(bitstring, bitstring).                     (* a client: the kind it dials, the bytes it sends *)
event ServedKind(bitstring, bitstring).                (* an agent: its service's kind, the bytes its service got *)
event ClientDgram(bitstring, bitstring).               (* session key, datagram: sent on its direct connection *)
event AgentDgram(bitstring, bitstring).                (* session key, datagram: handed to the session's flow *)

(* The client's direct path for its session k: the relay hands it an
   address (cand); whoever the attacker routes there answers with a
   certificate and a key (the QUIC handshake, TLS 1.3 as for the session).
   direct-no-cert-check: the answer's certificate is not checked;
   direct-no-token: the agent's token is not checked; token-unbound: the
   tokens bind the session but not the direct QUIC key; token-no-role:
   both ends send the same token (no role in it or its message). *)
let DirectClient(k: bitstring, want: bitstring, grouped: bool, kind: bitstring) =
  in(c, cand: bitstring);
  let ls = labS in (* NOT:token-no-role *)
  let ls = labC in (* ONLY:token-no-role *)
  in(c, (dcert: bitstring, dpk: pkey));
  let (dn: bitstring, dg: bitstring, =dpk, ds: bitstring, de: bitstring) = checksign(dcert, pk(orgk)) in (* NOT:direct-no-cert-check *)
  let (dn: bitstring, dg: bitstring, =dpk, ds: bitstring, de: bitstring) = getmsg(dcert) in (* ONLY:direct-no-cert-check *)
  if directNameOK(dn, dg, want, grouped) then (* NOT:direct-no-cert-check *)
  if de = live then (* NOT:direct-no-cert-check *)
  if ds <> serWebRev && ds <> serLost then (* NOT:direct-no-cert-check *)
  new kd: bitstring;
  out(c, aenc(kd, dpk));
  let tokC = h((k, kd, labC, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* NOT:token-unbound *)
  let tokS = h((k, kd, ls, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* NOT:token-unbound *)
  let tokC = h((k, labC, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* ONLY:token-unbound *)
  let tokS = h((k, ls, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* ONLY:token-unbound *)
  event ClientDirectOffer(k, kd);
  out(c, senc((labC, tokC), kd));
  in(c, x: bitstring);
  let (=ls, =tokS) = sdec(x, kd) in (* NOT:direct-no-token *)
  event ClientDirect(k, kd, ds);
  event DirectTaken(k, kd, dn, want, grouped);
  out(c, senc(dirData, kd));
  (* a datagram session's datagram on that connection: a QUIC DATAGRAM
     frame under its keys, its tag naming the attach (BIND:dgram.tag) *)
  if kind = kindDg then
  event ClientDgram(k, dgData);
  out(c, senc((labD, dgData), kd)).

(* The client's relayed re-attaches of its session k: the direct path (or
   the previous relayed stream) died, so a new relayed stream, OPEN(epoch,
   tokR), then the session's records on it. *)
let ReAttach(k: bitstring, ns: bitstring) =
  event ClientAttach(k, ep2);
  out(c, (ep2, h((h((k, ns)), labC, tokEpoch(ep2)))));
  out(c, senc(attData, k));
  in(c, died: bitstring);                              (* the ep2 stream died too *)
  event ClientAttach(k, ep3);
  out(c, (ep3, h((h((k, ns)), labC, tokEpoch(ep3)))));
  out(c, senc(attData, k)).

(* Web's agent: its acceptor for epoch e of session k, on a new relayed
   stream. *)
let AttachAgent(k: bitstring, ns: bitstring, e: bitstring) =
  in(c, (=e, tok: bitstring));
  if tok = h((h((k, ns)), labC, tokEpoch(e))) then
  event AgentAttach(k, e).

(* Web's agent: a direct connection (its certificate, the session's key
   pair) bound to its session k only on that session's client token.
   agent-direct-no-token: bound on the relay's word (a session id). *)
let DirectAgent(k: bitstring, sk: skey, kind: bitstring) =
  in(c, ekd: bitstring);
  let ls = labS in (* NOT:token-no-role *)
  let ls = labC in (* ONLY:token-no-role *)
  let kd = adec(ekd, sk) in
  let tokC = h((k, kd, labC, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* NOT:token-unbound *)
  let tokS = h((k, kd, ls, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* NOT:token-unbound *)
  let tokC = h((k, labC, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* ONLY:token-unbound *)
  let tokS = h((k, ls, tokEpoch(ep1))) in (* ONLY:token-unbound *)
  (if kind = kindDg then in(c, y: bitstring); let (=labD, m: bitstring) = sdec(y, kd) in event AgentDgram(k, m)) | ( (* ONLY:dgram-tag-unbound *)
  in(c, x: bitstring);
  let (=labC, =tokC) = sdec(x, kd) in (* NOT:agent-direct-no-token *)
  event AgentDirect(k, kd);
  out(c, senc((ls, tokS), kd)); (* NOT:dgram-tag-unbound *)
  (* a datagram is handed to session k only on a connection bound to k *)
  if kind = kindDg then (* NOT:dgram-tag-unbound *)
  in(c, y: bitstring); let (=labD, m: bitstring) = sdec(y, kd) in event AgentDgram(k, m). (* NOT:dgram-tag-unbound *)
  out(c, senc((ls, tokS), kd))). (* ONLY:dgram-tag-unbound *)

(* The client, enrolled: names machine web and its service svc (pg or
   vault), sends data, organisation mode whatever the relay answers. *)
let Client(certCli: bitstring, svc: bitstring, kind: bitstring, payload: bitstring) =
  event Dialled(nameWeb, svc, payload);
  event Dials(kind, payload);
  out(c, (nameWeb, true));                             (* the open: web's service, E2Ee *)
  in(c, answer: bitstring);
  if answer = answerPlain then out(c, payload) else (* ONLY:downgrade-plain *)
  if answer = answerOK then
  let offer = alpnM(kind, nameWeb, svc) in
  out(c, offer);                                       (* ClientHello: ALPN *)
  in(c, (scert: bitstring, spk: pkey, ns: bitstring)); (* the session's certificate, key and server random *)
  let (sn: bitstring, sg: bitstring, =spk, ss: bitstring, se: bitstring) = checksign(scert, pk(orgk)) in (* NOT:client-no-chain-check *)
  let (sn: bitstring, sg: bitstring, =spk, ss: bitstring, se: bitstring) = getmsg(scert) in (* ONLY:client-no-chain-check *)
  if sn = nameWeb then                                 (* the name it asked for *) (* NOT:no-name-check *)
  if se = live then                                    (* NotAfter *) (* NOT:client-no-expiry-check *)
  if ss <> serWebRev && ss <> serLost then             (* the CRL *) (* NOT:client-no-crl-check *)
  event ClientAccepted(ss);
  new k: bitstring;
  out(c, aenc((k, ns), spk));                          (* the key exchange, bound to the server random (the transcript) *)
  in(c, ee: bitstring);
  let (=eeTag, np: bitstring) = sdec(ee, k) in
  if np = offer then                                   (* the negotiated protocol is the offer *) (* NOT:client-no-alpn-check *)
  out(c, (certCli, sign(h((k, spk)), skCli)));          (* Certificate + CertificateVerify *)
  (DirectClient(k, nameWeb, false, kind)) | (ReAttach(k, ns)) | (
  event ClientSent(serCli, payload);
  out(c, senc((c2s, appData, payload), k));
  in(c, appAbort: bool);                               (* the local application ends cleanly or resets: either *)
  if appAbort = true then (
    event AppAborted(serCli, payload);
    0                                                  (* Pump: tlsSession.Reset, no close_notify *) (* NOT:client-abort-as-close *)
    event ClientEnded(serCli, payload); (* ONLY:client-abort-as-close *)
    out(c, senc((c2s, closeAlert, payload), k)) (* ONLY:client-abort-as-close *)
  ) else
  event AppEnded(serCli, payload);
  event ClientEnded(serCli, payload);
  out(c, senc((c2s, closeAlert, payload), k));
  in(c, e: bitstring);
  let (=s2c, =appData, r: bitstring) = sdec(e, k) in (* NOT:agreement-without-key-check *)
  in(c, r: bitstring); (* ONLY:agreement-without-key-check *)
  event ClientRecv(k, r);
  in(c, e2: bitstring);
  if e2 = rawEnd then (
    0                                                  (* a reset to the local application *) (* NOT:clear-end *)
    event ClientCleanEnd(k, r) (* ONLY:clear-end *)
  ) else
  let (=s2c, =closeAlert, =r) = sdec(e2, k) in
  event ClientCleanEnd(k, r)).

(* The group-dial client, enrolled: pg@db, any machine of group db the
   relay routes to; no name. *)
let GClient(certCli: bitstring) =
  event Dials(kindS, gData);
  out(c, (svcPg, grpDb, true));                        (* the open: pg@db, E2Ee *)
  in(c, answer: bitstring);
  if answer = answerOK then
  let offer = alpnG(kindS, svcPg, grpDb) in
  out(c, offer);
  in(c, (scert: bitstring, spk: pkey, ns: bitstring));
  let (sn: bitstring, sg: bitstring, =spk, ss: bitstring, se: bitstring) = checksign(scert, pk(orgk)) in
  if sg = grpDb then                                   (* OU contains the group *) (* NOT:group-dial-no-group-check *)
  if se = live then
  if ss <> serWebRev && ss <> serLost then
  new k: bitstring;
  out(c, aenc((k, ns), spk));                          (* the key exchange, bound to the server random (the transcript) *)
  in(c, ee: bitstring);
  let (=eeTag, np: bitstring) = sdec(ee, k) in
  if np = offer then (* NOT:client-no-alpn-check *)
  out(c, (certCli, sign(h((k, spk)), skCli)));
  (DirectClient(k, sn, true, kindS)) | (
  event ClientSent(serCli, gData);
  out(c, senc((c2s, appData, gData), k));
  in(c, e: bitstring);
  let (=s2c, =appData, r: bitstring) = sdec(e, k) in
  event GClientRecv(k, r)).

(* Web's agent: a tcp service in organisation mode, allow_group db. fixed:
   the agent has a target of its own (a service table, --forward); a
   tunnel without one is refused at New (ErrE2EENoFixedTarget), modelled
   as an agent that serves nothing. relay-names-target: before E2EEPROOF
   finding 1's fix, that agent dialled the open's target. The session is
   routed to service svc, which the agent publishes under pub (noGroup:
   none), on machine name with key sk and certificate certWeb (OU ou). *)
let Agent(certWeb: bitstring, sk: skey, name: bitstring, ou: bitstring, svc: bitstring, kind: bitstring, pub: bitstring, fixed: bool) =
  event Publishes(name, svc, pub);
  in(c, (target: bitstring, e2ee: bool));
  if e2ee = true then                                  (* a plain session is refused *)
  in(c, offer: bitstring);                             (* ClientHello: ALPN *)
  if alpnOK(offer, kind, name, svc, pub, ou) then            (* else no_application_protocol *) (* NOT:agent-no-alpn-check *)
  let t0 = if fixed then svcAddr else target in (* ONLY:relay-names-target *)
  if fixed = true then (* NOT:relay-names-target *)
  let t0 = svcAddr in (* NOT:relay-names-target *)
  let t = t0 in (* NOT:relay-names-target-with-forward *)
  let t = target in (* ONLY:relay-names-target-with-forward *)
  new ns: bitstring;                                   (* ServerHello.random *)
  out(c, (certWeb, pk(sk), ns));
  in(c, ek: bitstring);
  let (k: bitstring, =ns) = adec(ek, sk) in           (* a handshake replayed to another session fails *)
  out(c, senc((eeTag, offer), k));                     (* EncryptedExtensions: the protocol it chose *)
  in(c, (ccert: bitstring, cv: bitstring));
  if ccert = noCert then (in(c, e0: bitstring); let (=c2s, =appData, m0: bitstring) = sdec(e0, k) in event ServiceGot(noCert, m0); out(c, senc((s2c, appData, svcData), k))) else (* ONLY:downgrade-any-client *)
  let (cn: bitstring, cg: bitstring, cpk: pkey, cs: bitstring, ce: bitstring) = checksign(ccert, pk(orgk)) in (* NOT:agent-no-chain-check *)
  let (cn: bitstring, cg: bitstring, cpk: pkey, cs: bitstring, ce: bitstring) = getmsg(ccert) in (* ONLY:agent-no-chain-check *)
  if cg = grpDb then                                   (* allow_group *) (* NOT:no-group-check *)
  if ce = live then                                    (* NotAfter *) (* NOT:agent-no-expiry-check *)
  if cs <> serWebRev && cs <> serLost then             (* the CRL *) (* NOT:agent-no-crl-check *)
  if checksign(cv, cpk) = h((k, pk(sk))) then       (* CertificateVerify (crypto/tls) *) (* NOT:skip-certificate-verify *)
  (DirectAgent(k, sk, kind)) | (AttachAgent(k, ns, ep2)) | (AttachAgent(k, ns, ep3)) | (
  in(c, e: bitstring);
  let (=c2s, =appData, m: bitstring) = sdec(e, k) in
  if t = svcAddr then (
    event ServiceGot(cs, m);                           (* to its own service, on its machine *)
    event Served(name, svc, m);
    event ServedKind(kind, m);
    new r: bitstring;
    event AgentSent(k, (r, svcData));
    out(c, senc((s2c, appData, (r, svcData)), k));
    in(c, targetAbort: bool);                          (* the target ends cleanly or resets: either *)
    if targetAbort = true then (
      event TargetAborted(k, (r, svcData));
      0                                                (* Join: tlsend Conn.Reset, no close_notify *) (* NOT:abort-as-close *)
      event AgentEnded(k, (r, svcData)); (* ONLY:abort-as-close *)
      out(c, senc((s2c, closeAlert, (r, svcData)), k)) (* ONLY:abort-as-close *)
    ) else
    event TargetEnded(k, (r, svcData));
    event AgentEnded(k, (r, svcData));
    out(c, senc((s2c, closeAlert, (r, svcData)), k));
    in(c, e2: bitstring);
    if e2 = rawEnd then (
      0                                                (* the target reset *) (* NOT:agent-clear-end *)
      event ServiceCleanEnd(cs, m) (* ONLY:agent-clear-end *)
    ) else
    let (=c2s, =closeAlert, =m) = sdec(e2, k) in
    event ServiceCleanEnd(cs, m)                       (* the target's half close *)
  ) else
    out(c, (t, m))).                                   (* dialTarget: another host, the attacker's *)

(* 1. the client's bytes reach only machine web's own service: not eve
   (another name), not a certificate the relay made, not web's expired or
   revoked key, not in plain on the relay's word, not a target the relay
   names (mutants client-no-chain-check, no-name-check,
   client-no-expiry-check, client-no-crl-check, downgrade-plain,
   relay-names-target, relay-names-target-with-forward) *)
(* expect true *)
query attacker(payload).
(* 2. what the client takes as web's answer, web's agent sent in that
   session (mutant agreement-without-key-check) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; inj-event(ClientRecv(k, r)) ==> inj-event(AgentSent(k, r)).
(* 3, 4, 5. the server certificates the client refuses: another name, revoked, expired *)
(* expect true *)
query event(ClientAccepted(serEve)).
(* expect true *)
query event(ClientAccepted(serWebRev)).
(* expect true *)
query event(ClientAccepted(serWebOld)).
(* 6. the service's answer reaches only an admitted client (mutants
   agent-no-chain-check, no-group-check, agent-no-expiry-check,
   agent-no-crl-check, skip-certificate-verify, downgrade-any-client: a
   service that serves a client without an organisation certificate) *)
(* expect true *)
query attacker(svcData).
(* 7. what reaches the service was sent by an admitted client *)
(* expect true *)
query s: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(ServiceGot(s, m)) ==> event(ClientSent(s, m)).
(* 8, 9, 10. the clients the service refuses: outside its group, revoked, expired *)
(* expect true *)
query m: bitstring; event(ServiceGot(serEve, m)).
(* expect true *)
query m: bitstring; event(ServiceGot(serLost, m)).
(* expect true *)
query m: bitstring; event(ServiceGot(serOld, m)).
(* 11. a clean end the client passes on was the agent's close_notify: the
   relay cutting the stream between two records is a reset (CLAIMS-A Q5;
   mutant clear-end: crypto/tls's io.EOF taken as a clean end) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; event(ClientCleanEnd(k, r)) ==> event(AgentEnded(k, r)).
(* 12. likewise toward the service: its half close was the client's
   (mutant agent-clear-end) *)
(* expect true *)
query s: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(ServiceCleanEnd(s, m)) ==> event(ClientEnded(s, m)).
(* 13. a clean end at the client was the target's: its reset reaches the
   client as a reset (lane TCPRESET, mutant abort-as-close) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; event(ClientCleanEnd(k, r)) ==> event(TargetEnded(k, r)).
(* 14. the service's half close was the client's local application's clean
   end (mutant client-abort-as-close) *)
(* expect true *)
query s: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(ServiceCleanEnd(s, m)) ==> event(AppEnded(s, m)).
(* 15, 16. witnesses: an allowed client reaches the service, and gets its answer *)
(* expect false *)
query m: bitstring; event(ServiceGot(serCli, m)).
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; event(ClientRecv(k, r)).
(* 17, 18. witnesses: both clean ends happen *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; event(ClientCleanEnd(k, r)).
(* expect false *)
query s: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(ServiceCleanEnd(s, m)).
(* 19, 20. witnesses: both aborts happen *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; event(TargetAborted(k, r)).
(* expect false *)
query s: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(AppAborted(s, m)).

(* 21. what the client sends on a direct connection it took reaches only
   web's agent: the relay's address cannot put another holder there
   (mutants direct-no-cert-check, and with direct-no-token too) *)
(* expect true *)
query attacker(dirData).
(* 22. a direct connection the client takes ends at web's agent, bound to
   the client's own session (mutants direct-no-token, token-unbound) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring, s: bitstring; inj-event(ClientDirect(k, kd, s)) ==> inj-event(AgentDirect(k, kd)).
(* 23. the agent binds a direct connection to a session only for that
   session's client (mutant agent-direct-no-token) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring; event(AgentDirect(k, kd)) ==> event(ClientDirectOffer(k, kd)).
(* 24. the client takes no other machine's certificate on the direct path *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring; event(ClientDirect(k, kd, serEve)).
(* 25, 26. witnesses: the client takes a direct connection; the agent binds one *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring, s: bitstring; event(ClientDirect(k, kd, s)).
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring; event(AgentDirect(k, kd)).

(* 27. the agent attaches a stream at epoch e of a session only on that
   session's client's OPEN for e, once each (mutant token-no-epoch: the
   relay replays ep2's OPEN as ep3's) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, e: bitstring; inj-event(AgentAttach(k, e)) ==> inj-event(ClientAttach(k, e)).
(* 28. what the client sends on a re-attached relayed stream stays secret,
   replayed or not: a replay is a denial only (holds under token-no-epoch) *)
(* expect true *)
query attacker(attData).
(* 29. witness: the agent attaches a relayed re-attach *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring; event(AgentAttach(k, ep3)).

(* Services by name (lane SVCBIND). 30. what the group-dial client sends
   for pg@db reaches no one outside group db (mutant
   group-dial-no-group-check) *)
(* expect true *)
query attacker(gData).
(* 31. ... and only a service its machine publishes under db: not web's
   vault, not mal's pg published under ops (mutants agent-no-alpn-check,
   agent-no-publish-check, client-no-alpn-check) *)
(* expect true *)
query n: bitstring, s: bitstring; event(Served(n, s, gData)) ==> event(Publishes(n, s, grpDb)).
(* 32. injective agreement for the group dial *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; inj-event(GClientRecv(k, r)) ==> inj-event(AgentSent(k, r)).
(* 33. a machine dial reaches only the named agent's named service: the
   relay cannot route web/pg to web's vault (mutants client-no-alpn-check,
   agent-no-alpn-check) *)
(* expect true *)
query n: bitstring, s: bitstring; event(Served(n, s, payload)) ==> event(Dialled(n, s, payload)).
(* 34, 35. witnesses: the group dial completes; the second service serves *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, r: bitstring; event(GClientRecv(k, r)).
(* expect false *)
query m: bitstring; event(Served(nameWeb, svcVault, m)).

(* Direct paths under a group dial (lane DIRECTGROUP). 36. a direct
   connection a client takes names the machine of its session: the relay
   cannot move a group dial's session to another instance (mutant
   group-direct-no-name-check with direct-no-token) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring, dn: bitstring, w: bitstring, g: bool; event(DirectTaken(k, kd, dn, w, g)) ==> dn = w.
(* 37. witness: a group dial's session goes direct *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, kd: bitstring, dn: bitstring, w: bitstring; event(DirectTaken(k, kd, dn, w, true)).

(* Datagram services (lane UDP1). 38. a datagram a client sends on a
   direct connection it took reaches only web's agent *)
(* expect true *)
query attacker(dgData).
(* 39. the agent hands a datagram to session k only if k's own client sent
   it, on a connection bound to k (mutant dgram-tag-unbound); not
   injective: a replayed packet is QUIC's to discard (RFC 9000 12.3) *)
(* expect true *)
query k: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(AgentDgram(k, m)) ==> event(ClientDgram(k, m)).
(* 40, 41. witnesses: a client sends a datagram direct; the agent hands one on *)
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(ClientDgram(k, m)).
(* expect false *)
query k: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(AgentDgram(k, m)).
(* 42. what reaches a service of a kind was dialled with that kind: the
   relay cannot route a stream client to the datagram service of the same
   name, or the reverse (mutants agent-ignores-kind, client-no-alpn-check) *)
(* expect true *)
query kd: bitstring, m: bitstring; event(ServedKind(kd, m)) ==> event(Dials(kd, m)).
(* 43. witness: the datagram client reaches the datagram service *)
(* expect false *)
query m: bitstring; event(ServedKind(kindDg, m)).

process
  new skEve: skey; new skLost: skey; new skOld: skey; new skWebOld: skey; new skWebRev: skey;
  let certWeb = sign((nameWeb, grpDb, pk(skWeb), serWeb, live), orgk) in
  let certCli = sign((nameCli, grpDb, pk(skCli), serCli, live), orgk) in
  let certMal = sign((nameMal, grpDb, pk(skMal), serMal, live), orgk) in
  out(c, certWeb); out(c, certCli); out(c, certMal);
  out(c, (skEve, sign((nameEve, grpWeb, pk(skEve), serEve, live), orgk)));
  out(c, (skLost, sign((nameLost, grpDb, pk(skLost), serLost, live), orgk)));
  out(c, (skOld, sign((nameOld, grpDb, pk(skOld), serOld, expired), orgk)));
  out(c, (skWebOld, sign((nameWeb, grpWeb, pk(skWebOld), serWebOld, expired), orgk)));
  out(c, (skWebRev, sign((nameWeb, grpWeb, pk(skWebRev), serWebRev, live), orgk)));
  ((!Agent(certWeb, skWeb, nameWeb, grpDb, svcPg, kindS, grpDb, true)) | (!Agent(certWeb, skWeb, nameWeb, grpDb, svcPg, kindS, grpDb, false)) |
   (!Agent(certWeb, skWeb, nameWeb, grpDb, svcVault, kindS, noGroup, true)) | (!Agent(certMal, skMal, nameMal, grpDb, svcPg, kindS, grpOps, true)) |
   (!Agent(certWeb, skWeb, nameWeb, grpDb, svcPg, kindDg, grpDb, true)) |
   (!Client(certCli, svcPg, kindS, payload)) | (!Client(certCli, svcVault, kindS, vData)) | (!Client(certCli, svcPg, kindDg, uData)) | (!GClient(certCli)))
